* Five-transistor OTA in unity gain with an on-chip mirror bias
* The tail bias is generated by a diode-connected device rather than supplied
* as a gate voltage, so both the bias point and the loop solution are the
* model's to find. No .ic card: transients start from the DC operating point.
<MODEL_SETUP>
.temp <TEMP>
Vdd vdd 0 <VDD>
Vin vin 0 <BUFFER_IN>
Ibias vdd nbias <IBIAS_CELL>
<N_PREFIX>n_bias nbias nbias 0 0 <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_tail tail nbias 0 0 <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_l n1 vin tail 0 <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_r vout vout tail 0 <N_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_l n1 n1 vdd vdd <P_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_r vout n1 vdd vdd <P_DEVICE>
CL vout 0 <CL>
<ANALYSIS>
.end
